  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of life-saving water, sanitation and hygiene services to disaster-affected people in South-West, Hirshabelle and Galmudug states andMiddle Shabelle region in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to save lives, prevent disease outbreaks, and mitigate displacement by delivering comprehensive Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH) services to communities impacted by disasters in Somalia. By addressing the effects of calamities such as droughts, floods, and conflicts in regions already identified by UNOCHA as priority like Southwest (Baidoa/ Qansaxdhere), Hirshabele (Beletweyne), Middle Shabelle (Jowhar) and Galmudug (Galkayo), this project aligns with broader humanitarian efforts to reduce disaster-related suffering.</narrative>
  </description>
